# Macros named *_MAX_* or *_LIMIT* that are not limits a user can reach, so they have no row in SIFT_LIMITS (src/core/limits.h).
# NAME, a tab, the reason. scripts/gen-limits.sh --check fails for a macro that is neither here nor a row, and for a line whose macro is gone.
# A bound that a user can reach gets a row, not a line here.
ARR_MAX_CANDS	array columns whose elements the default of paths samples: a memory bound of the sample (128 MB of sets), the others keep their image
CHUNK_MAX_N	sanity bound on the row count a decoder reads from a chunk: a corruption check
ESTIMATE_MEMO_MAX_KEY	size of the key of a planner memo: an internal cache bound with no visible effect
MERGE_MAX_BYTES	no caller left: delete it in a cleanup
ORDER_MAX_ROWS	the most rows of a key-cut unit, the maximum of sift.col_unit_rows (the directory of a unit is read with the head of its record)
PAGG_MAX_TUPLES	decoder bound for a rollup blob (a corruption check), derived from rollup_tuples
POOL_MAX_BLOCKS	size of the CREATE INDEX buffer pool, kept so that addresses stay below 2^32 (sift.test_pool_blocks lowers it)
SIFT_ALLOC_MAX_LOCKED	invariant of the block allocator, not reachable by valid input
SIFT_COL_FORMAT_MAX_READ	the newest column format minor this build reads: a version, not a size
SIFT_COL_MAX_LANES	array size of the lanes of one numeric leaf
SIFT_CORDER_MAX_KEYS	an IN list of more keys than this is read from the units: each key seeks a chunk of the sorted keys of its own
SIFT_CORDER_MAX_ROWS	a range of more rows than this is read from the units: the addresses of a range are sorted by position before the heap is read
SIFT_CPOINT_MAX_KEYS	keys of one lookup that the point directory answers: a speed threshold, the answer is the same either way
SIFT_CPOINT_MAX_RANGE	keys of one range that the point directory enumerates: a speed threshold, the zones answer a longer range the same way
SIFT_CPOINT_MAX_ROWS	rows of one lookup that the point directory answers: a speed threshold, the answer is the same either way
SIFT_FOLD_MAX_EXPAND	characters one character expands to in case folding: a property of the Unicode tables
SIFT_FSM_SWEEP_MAX_PCT	the share of the index the orphan sweep may free (core/f2/fsm/sweep.c): over it the sweep names a reference it missed and frees nothing; no setting names it
SIFT_HYB_ACL_MAX_KEYS	the keys a set of the hybrid semi join holds: the value of SIFT_SEMI_MAX_SET, whose row names the limit
SIFT_MAX_EXTENTS	derived from the page layout (extents of a segment header)
SIFT_MAX_OFF	width of a page bitmap: the layout of the postings
SIFT_MAX_OFFSET	MaxHeapTuplesPerPage, a PostgreSQL bound
SIFT_MAX_REBINDS	size of the table of kernel rebind callbacks
SIFT_MAX_W	words of a page bitmap: the layout of the postings
SIFT_MERGE_MAX_FANIN	merge policy: segments one merge reads at a time
SIFT_MERGE_MAX_SEGMENTS	merge policy: more directory entries than this start a merge
SIFT_RADIX_MAX_DIGIT	bits of the widest digit of the radix sort of core/cmp.h: the counters of a digit (4 KB) and the cache lines its pass writes to; the order of the result does not depend on it
SIFT_SRC_MAX_DIMS	planner-side array size of the dimensions of a source, above cube_dims
SIFT_SRC_MAX_MEAS	planner-side array size that mirrors cube_measures
SIFT_SRC_MAX_RDIMS	planner-side array size that mirrors rollup_dims
SIFT_SRC_MAX_ROLLUPS	planner-side array size that mirrors rollups
SIFT_TBL_MAX_OFF	MaxHeapTuplesPerPage, a PostgreSQL bound
SIFT_TBL_MAX_WBUF_PAGES	array size of the page list of one write buffer: see write_buffer_kb and tx_write_buffers
SIFT_TBL_ROW_MAX_INLINE	a sift_table row above half a page goes to overflow pages: a layout threshold, not a limit
SIFT_KTAB_MAX_GROUPS	the keys of a leaf in a segment beyond which the accumulator of its key table stops: a memory bound, a table that large takes more than 3% of any segment
VK_MAX_MEMORY_HEAPS	constant of the Vulkan API
VK_MAX_MEMORY_TYPES	constant of the Vulkan API
VK_MAX_PHYSICAL_DEVICE_NAME_SIZE	constant of the Vulkan API
LOAD_MAX_GROUPS	groups a bulk load writes at once: the backend and three workers, bounded by max_parallel_maintenance_workers and maintenance_work_mem
LOAD_MAX_UNITS	array size of the units of a run: LOAD_SBS for each of LOAD_MAX_GROUPS
SIFT_CONN_MAX_CONNECTIONS	connections one connect option names: a syntax bound of the option text, rejected with an error
CONN_TAGS_MAX_KEYS	the keys of a read past which its journal records are not filtered by their key tag (the tags of that many keys leave few records out): a cost bound, the rows are the same
BLK_SLOTS	layout: the offsets of one scoring block, SIFT_BLK_PAGES pages of SIFT_KERN_SLOTS
SIFT_KERN_SLOTS	layout: the offsets of one heap page in the offset mask (SIFT_OFFMASK_WORDS words of 64 bits)
CUBE_SET_SLOTS	size of the probe table of one histogram dimension, a power of two over twice its groups (col/v1/keycols/cube.c); the table is local to the call
ROWS_SLOTS	size of the probe table that counts the distinct pairs of a stretch, a power of two over the cells a unit may keep; it stops counting at its limit
F_SLOTS	a flag bit of a shared dictionary (the slots form), not a size
KEYS_DENSE_SLOTS	slots a key needs in a bitmap before a sorted array is used instead: a speed threshold, the keys are the same
PEND_SLOTS	indexes whose rows a backend buffers for one commit (col/v1/wbuf/pending.c): the rows of another index are written to its lane at once
SET_MEMO_SLOTS	entries of the memo of the ranges of one probe, replaced in turn (col/v1/amscan/ranges.c)
TOMB_SLOTS	indexes whose tombstones a statement holds back for the page-wise append (col/v1/supersede.c): when none is free every held buffer goes to the log and the first is reused
SIFT_TOMB_PRESSURE_ENTRIES	the length of the tombstone log of a sift_table at which the maintenance worker is asked for: a scheduling threshold, with no effect on what a statement may do
SIFT_TOMB_SYNC_ENTRIES	the length of the tombstone log of a sift_table past which a ticking backend leaves the count of its tombstones to the worker: a scheduling threshold, with no effect on what a statement may do
REFILL_SAMPLE_ENTRIES	the entries of each sampled unit that go to the sample of the key ranges of a refill sort (col/v1/maint/scope.c): the size of a sample, the ranges only come out less even from a smaller one
SIFT_COL_BTREE_WORKERS	participants of a build through a btree on the key at most (the directory holds the segments of each): a share of the directory, not a size a table may reach (col/v1/build/btree_par.c)
SIM_MAX_BLOCKS	blocks the cache of the choice between the btree and the key ranges simulates at most (the cache is scaled down by a power of two to it): bounds the memory of the walk, not what a table may hold (col/v1/build/btree_pick.c)
COST_MIN_US	the range (microseconds) a measured cost of a read of the heap is held to by the choice between a btree on the key and the key ranges (col/v1/build/btree_probe.c): a read of a page in the memory of the system and a seek of a disk that spins; a noise bound of the measurement, not a size a table may reach
COST_MAX_US	the upper end of that range
PRICE_BYTES	bytes of rows the pricing of the key ranges' files may take (col/v1/build/spill.c): bounds the memory of the pricing, not what a table may reach
WORKER_SLOTS	slots of the table of running workers in shared memory (core/worker.c): the maximum of sift.max_maint_workers, which docs/OPTIONS.md lists with the setting
SIFT_CACHE_MAX_KINDS	the table of the kinds of cache that register with the backend cache budget: one row for each cache of the source tree, fixed when the code is
SIFT_MEM_MAX_BLOCK	the largest block (256 kB) a transient allocation of a tracked context takes, so that freeing it returns whole blocks to the allocator
SIFT_PART_LOCK_SLOTS	the virtual page locks of the partitions of a relation (core/part_lock.h): a part id is taken modulo it, so two partitions may share a lock and wait for each other; no count is refused
SIFT_UNIQUE_LOCK_SLOTS	the virtual page locks of the keys of a unique index (core/part_lock.h): the hash of a key is taken modulo it, so two keys may share a lock and wait for each other; no count is refused
SIFT_SHM_MANIFEST_SLOTS	the slots of the manifest registry (core/shm/manifest.h): an index the registry has no slot for is read from its pages, and the least used slot is given up; no count is refused
SIFT_F2_MAX_RANGES	key ranges of one predicate that the zones of a part prune: a speed threshold, the rows are the same
SIFT_FSM_CLASS_QUEUE	the tag of the queue of released extents among the lists of the allocator (a list is told by it), not a bound
SIFT_FSM_MAX_EXTENT	the largest size class of the allocator of format major 2: derived from the number of classes
SIFT_TAIL_MAX_PIECES	the extents the free space below a cut may be cut into for the pieces of a part that move below it (col/f2/tail_plan.h): a free space in more pieces would give the part more extents than the file gains
SIFT_FSM_MAX_SLABS	the metadata slabs the root page of the allocator holds (core/fsm.h): a bound of the page layout, each slab holds 256 metadata pages
SIFT_L0_SLAB_MAX_PAGES	the pages of the L0 slab of a partition (col/l0_slab.h): a micro-part is made from the slab before it grows past it, so no table reaches it
SIFT_NULL_SPARSE_MAX_DIV	the share of nulls from which a list of them is not written: an encoding choice with no visible effect
SIFT_PARTDIR_MAX_LEVEL	the levels of the partition directory above its leaves (core/manifest.h): a bound of the page layout, millions of partitions away
SIFT_QSET_SLOTS	the relations the shared set of quarantined indexes holds (core/quarantine/set.h): past it the quarantine is refused with a hint to REINDEX
SIFT_FSST_MAX_PERMILLE	the share of its raw bytes a string chunk may take coded for the coding to be kept: a size choice of the writer, the strings read back are the same
SIFT_FSST_MAX_SYMBOLS	array size of the symbol table of a string chunk: a property of the coding, not a setting
SIFT_META_INLINE_MAX_PARTS	the parts of a partition that its manifest entry keeps inline: a layout threshold, the rows are the same either way
SIFT_TRIGRAM_MAX_BLOCKS	the most blocks of the substring filter of one granule: a size bound of a summary, a granule that needs more keeps none and is read
SIFT_ALP_RD_MAX_LEFT	the widest left part (bits) of a split of a double in the ALP RD coding of a granule: a property of the coding, the values read back are the same
SIFT_MAX_PART_LEVEL	the levels of the parts of a partition above level 0 (col/f2/compact/compact.h): a compaction policy, no part is rewritten past it and the rows are the same
SIFT_VSTR_MAX_STEPS	array size of the steps of one text program: held by an assertion where a step is added
AK6_GID_MAX_NOSEL	tuning bound of an algorithm (memory, batch or radix size, load factor): it changes the speed or memory of a plan, not its rows
BIAS_LIMIT	tuning bound of an algorithm (memory, batch or radix size, load factor): it changes the speed or memory of a plan, not its rows
DENSE_MAX_GROUPS	the most items (columns, keys, filters, masks, operations) one scan node handles: a statement with more is not planned by the scan and PostgreSQL plans it, the rows are the same
DIS_MAX_LEVEL	tuning bound of an algorithm (memory, batch or radix size, load factor): it changes the speed or memory of a plan, not its rows
DIST_MAX_CHUNK	tuning bound of an algorithm (memory, batch or radix size, load factor): it changes the speed or memory of a plan, not its rows
F2_AUTO_SLOTS	slots of a fixed internal table or shared array: a capacity of the implementation that a full table handles by waiting or falling back, not a limit on a statement
GJ_MAX_CHUNK	tuning bound of an algorithm (memory, batch or radix size, load factor): it changes the speed or memory of a plan, not its rows
MAX_SLOTS	slots of a fixed internal table or shared array: a capacity of the implementation that a full table handles by waiting or falling back, not a limit on a statement
SC_LOW_SPEED_LIMIT	tuning bound of an algorithm (memory, batch or radix size, load factor): it changes the speed or memory of a plan, not its rows
SIFT_ALPRD_MAX_TZ	bound of an on-disk or shared-memory record or of a decoder: a layout constant and a corruption check, not a limit a user can reach
SIFT_APIPE_MAX_OPS	the most items (columns, keys, filters, masks, operations) one scan node handles: a statement with more is not planned by the scan and PostgreSQL plans it, the rows are the same
SIFT_BATCH_MAX_ROWS	tuning bound of an algorithm (memory, batch or radix size, load factor): it changes the speed or memory of a plan, not its rows
